2026-06-04 15:35:33 [http-nio-8080-exec-1] DEBUG c.d.w.s.e.WikipediaIngestionService - Wikipedia API response body: {"batchcomplete":"","continue":{"grncontinue":"0.479188080130|0.479189372364|36812931|0","continue":"grncontinue||"},"query":{"pages":{"82064242":{"pageid":82064242,"ns":0,"title":"Amy Boleyn","extract":"Amata \"Amy\" Boleyn, Lady Calthorpe (cirka 1485–1543) often called Amy Boleyn, and sometimes incorrectly called Jane Boleyn, was an English noblewoman and courtier. She was the paternal aunt of queen Anne Boleyn and the royal governess of the future Mary I of England between 1521 and 1525."},"37740331":{"pageid":37740331,"ns":0,"title":"Physiological anisocoria","extract":"Physiological anisocoria is when human pupils differ in size. It is generally considered to be benign, though it must be distinguished from congenital Horner's syndrome, pharmacological dilatation, or other conditions connected to the sympathetic nervous system. The prevalence of physiological anisocoria has not been found to be influenced by the sex, age, or iris color of the subject."},"40580849":{"pageid":40580849,"ns":0,"title":"Yengejeh, Heris","extract":"Yengejeh (Persian: ينگجه; also known as Angija, Yengejeh Badostan, and Yengidzha) is a village in Bedevostan-e Gharbi Rural District, Khvajeh District, Heris County, East Azerbaijan Province, Iran. At the 2006 census, its population was 151, in 31 families."},"61465285":{"pageid":61465285,"ns":0,"title":"Mosharraf Hossain (Bogra politician)","extract":"Md Mosharrf Hossain is a Bangladesh Nationalist Party politician and a former Jatiya Sangsad member representing the Bogra-4 constituency during 2019–2022. He resigned from the position on 11 December 2022."},"73934224":{"pageid":73934224,"ns":0,"title":"Miyandaman Rural District","extract":"Miyandaman Rural District (Persian: دهستان میاندامان) is in Kuhestan District of Tonekabon County, Mazandaran province, Iran. Its capital is the village of Latak, whose population at the time of the 2016 National Census was 434 people in 140 households."},"57343526":{"pageid":57343526,"ns":0,"title":"Coquillettia albiclava","extract":"Coquillettia albiclava is a species of plant bug in the family Miridae. It is found in North America."},"4576222":{"pageid":4576222,"ns":0,"title":"Gail Goestenkors","extract":"Gail Ann Goestenkors (born February 26, 1963) is an American basketball coach who was most recently an assistant coach for the Kentucky Wildcats women's basketball team.\nShe is perhaps best known as the women's college basketball head coach of Duke University and the University of Texas at Austin. She led Duke from 1992 until 2007, when she was hired to replace the retiring Jody Conradt at Texas.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Gail_Goestenkors_Mar-12-2009.jpg/500px-Gail_Goestenkors_Mar-12-2009.jpg","width":500,"height":531},"pageimage":"Gail_Goestenkors_Mar-12-2009.jpg"},"30792583":{"pageid":30792583,"ns":0,"title":"Eurypteryx bhaga","extract":"Eurypteryx bhaga, the hook-winged hawkmoth, is a moth of the family Sphingidae first described by Frederic Moore in 1866.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Eurypteryx_bhaga_MHNT_CUT_2010_0_27_Wang_Chin_District%2C_Phrae_Province%2C_Thailand_male_dorsal.jpg/500px-Eurypteryx_bhaga_MHNT_CUT_2010_0_27_Wang_Chin_District%2C_Phrae_Province%2C_Thailand_male_dorsal.jpg","width":500,"height":338},"pageimage":"Eurypteryx_bhaga_MHNT_CUT_2010_0_27_Wang_Chin_District,_Phrae_Province,_Thailand_male_dorsal.jpg"},"3274950":{"pageid":3274950,"ns":0,"title":"Kamyaran","extract":"Kamyaran (Persian: كامياران) is a city in the Central District of Kamyaran County, Kurdistan province, Iran, serving as capital of both the county and the district."},"56057629":{"pageid":56057629,"ns":0,"title":"Trichobranchidae","extract":"Trichobranchidae is a family of annelids in the order Terebellida.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Terebellides_horikoshii.jpg/500px-Terebellides_horikoshii.jpg","width":500,"height":375},"pageimage":"Terebellides_horikoshii.jpg"}}}}
