2026-06-04 15:41:56 [http-nio-8080-exec-3] DEBUG c.d.w.s.e.WikipediaIngestionService - Wikipedia API response body: {"batchcomplete":"","continue":{"grncontinue":"0.362584877998|0.362586202676|13658902|0","continue":"grncontinue||"},"query":{"pages":{"8463766":{"pageid":8463766,"ns":0,"title":"Olympiades station","extract":"Olympiades station (French pronunciation: [ɔlɛ̃pjad] ) is a station on Line 14 of the Paris Métro.\nThe station was formally inaugurated on 15 June 2007 in the presence of the Mayor of Paris, Bertrand Delanoë. It was opened to the general public at just before 5:30 a.m.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Station_Olympiades_M%C3%A9tro_Paris_Ligne_14_-_Paris_XIII_%28FR75%29_-_2022-07-02_-_5.jpg/500px-Station_Olympiades_M%C3%A9tro_Paris_Ligne_14_-_Paris_XIII_%28FR75%29_-_2022-07-02_-_5.jpg","width":500,"height":375},"pageimage":"Station_Olympiades_Métro_Paris_Ligne_14_-_Paris_XIII_(FR75)_-_2022-07-02_-_5.jpg"},"41193560":{"pageid":41193560,"ns":0,"title":"Yengi Arkh, Bijar","extract":"Yengi Arkh (Persian: ينگي ارخ, also Romanized as Yengī Arkh and Yangī Azakh) is a village in Gorgin Rural District, Korani District, Bijar County, Kurdistan Province, Iran. At the 2006 census, its population was 164, in 31 families. The village is populated by Azerbaijanis."},"3891835":{"pageid":3891835,"ns":0,"title":"Steganinae","extract":"The Steganinae Hendel, 1917, is the smaller of two subfamilies in the fruit fly family Drosophilidae. The other subfamily is the Drosophilinae.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Leucophenga_maculata_bl.jpg/500px-Leucophenga_maculata_bl.jpg","width":500,"height":408},"pageimage":"Leucophenga_maculata_bl.jpg"},"44175912":{"pageid":44175912,"ns":0,"title":"St James Parish Hall, Toowoomba","extract":"St James Parish Hall is a heritage-listed church hall at 112 Russell Street, Toowoomba, Queensland, Australia. It was designed by Henry James (Harry) Marks and built in 1912. It is also known as Taylor Memorial Institute.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/St_James_Parish_Hall%2C_Toowoomba.jpg/500px-St_James_Parish_Hall%2C_Toowoomba.jpg","width":500,"height":375},"pageimage":"St_James_Parish_Hall,_Toowoomba.jpg"},"2675837":{"pageid":2675837,"ns":0,"title":"The switch in time that saved nine","extract":"In U.S. Supreme Court history, \"The switch in time that saved nine\" is the phrase—originally a quip by humorist Cal Tinney—about what was perceived in 1937 as the sudden jurisprudential shift by Associate Justice Owen Roberts in the 1937 case West Coast Hotel Co. v. Parrish.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/96/Jowenroberts.jpg","width":304,"height":393},"pageimage":"Jowenroberts.jpg"},"18783132":{"pageid":18783132,"ns":0,"title":"Francis Turner (Royal Navy officer)","extract":"Admiral Sir Arthur Francis Turner  (23 June 1912 – 26 October 1991) was a British naval officer. He was the son of Rear Admiral AWJ Turner and his wife Mrs AM Turner (née Lochrane)."},"3357442":{"pageid":3357442,"ns":0,"title":"Going Blank Again","extract":"Going Blank Again is the second studio album by English rock band Ride, released on 9 March 1992 on Creation Records. It was produced by Alan Moulder, and peaked at No. 5 in the UK Albums Chart."},"63192031":{"pageid":63192031,"ns":0,"title":"John Petty Jr.","extract":"John Petty Jr. (born December 2, 1998) is an American professional basketball player. He played college basketball for the Alabama Crimson Tide.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e8/John_Petty_2020.jpg","width":360,"height":530},"pageimage":"John_Petty_2020.jpg"},"52973357":{"pageid":52973357,"ns":0,"title":"Iosu Goñi Leoz","extract":"Iosu Goñi Leoz (born 4 January 1990) is a Spanish handball player for Chambéry Savoie Mont-Blanc Handball and the Spanish team.\nHe participated at the 2017 World Men's Handball Championship.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Iosu_Goni_Leoz_20161005.jpg/500px-Iosu_Goni_Leoz_20161005.jpg","width":500,"height":794},"pageimage":"Iosu_Goni_Leoz_20161005.jpg"},"40005703":{"pageid":40005703,"ns":0,"title":"Kaleo (band)","extract":"Kaleo (stylized in all caps) is an Icelandic blues rock band which formed in Mosfellsbær in 2012. It consists of lead vocalist and guitarist Jökull Júlíusson, drummer Davíð Antonsson, bassist Daniel Kristjánsson, lead guitarist Rubin Pollock and harmonicist Þorleifur Gaukur Davíðsson. They have released four studio albums, Kaleo (2013), A/B (2016), Surface Sounds (2021), and Mixed Emotions (2025), as well as the EP Glasshouse (2013).","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/20180603_N%C3%BCrnberg_Rock_im_Park_Kaleo_0212.jpg/500px-20180603_N%C3%BCrnberg_Rock_im_Park_Kaleo_0212.jpg","width":500,"height":323},"pageimage":"20180603_Nürnberg_Rock_im_Park_Kaleo_0212.jpg"}}}}
