2026-06-04 15:43:33 [http-nio-8080-exec-4] DEBUG c.d.w.s.e.WikipediaIngestionService - Wikipedia API response body: {"batchcomplete":"","continue":{"grncontinue":"0.470499135533|0.470500662974|75225699|0","continue":"grncontinue||"},"query":{"pages":{"11706076":{"pageid":11706076,"ns":0,"title":"Stephen Varzaly","extract":"Stephen Varzaly (1890 – 1957) was a leading priest, journalist, and cultural activist for Rusyns in the United States."},"1960952":{"pageid":1960952,"ns":0,"title":"List of basketball players who have scored 100 points in a single game","extract":"In basketball, points are the sum of the score accumulated through field goals (two or three points) and free throws (one point). It is a rare achievement for an individual player to score 100 points in a single game. What follows is an incomplete list of all of the verified occurrences of players scoring 100 points or more.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Corey_Fisher_Villanova.jpg/500px-Corey_Fisher_Villanova.jpg","width":500,"height":1045},"pageimage":"Corey_Fisher_Villanova.jpg"},"82876784":{"pageid":82876784,"ns":0,"title":"Rockhill House Estate","extract":"Rockhill House Estate is a 17th-century country house and estate located in Letterkenny, County Donegal, Ireland. Historically the seat of the Stewart family and later an Irish Army post, the estate currently operates as a hotel, spa, and event venue. The property is recorded on the National Inventory of Architectural Heritage (NIAH reference 40906102) and the Donegal County Council Record of Protected Structures."},"58534655":{"pageid":58534655,"ns":0,"title":"Herbert Ellsworth Slaught","extract":"Herbert Ellsworth Slaught (1861–1937) was an American mathematician who was president of the Mathematical Association of America and editor of the journal American Mathematical Monthly.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/22/Herbert_Ellsworth_Slaught.jpg","width":246,"height":326},"pageimage":"Herbert_Ellsworth_Slaught.jpg"},"38795020":{"pageid":38795020,"ns":0,"title":"Viveca Hollmerus","extract":"Viveca Hollmerus, Lady Cable (1920–2004) was a Finnish-Swedish author. In 1951 she was awarded the Svenska Dagbladet Literature Prize, shared with Willy Kyrklund, Staffan Larsson and Per Anders Fogelstrom.\nIn 1954 she married the British diplomat Sir James Cable; they had one son.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/31/Viveca_Hollmerus_SFL.jpg","width":355,"height":458},"pageimage":"Viveca_Hollmerus_SFL.jpg"},"166950":{"pageid":166950,"ns":0,"title":"Aleksandër Stavre Drenova","extract":"Aleksandër Stavre Drenova (pronounced [alɛkˈsandəɾ staˈvɾɛ dɾɛˈnova]; 11 April 1872 – 11 December 1947), commonly known by the pen name Asdreni, was an Albanian poet, rilindas, translator, writer and the author of the poem which later became the national anthem of Albania. He is regarded as one of the most influential Albanian writers of the 20th century and composed most of his Albanian Renaissance-inspired known works during that period. \nBorn in the village of Drenovë, Asdreni completed his academic studies at the University of Bucharest in Romania where he enthusiastically committed himself to the Independence of Albania from the Ottoman Empire.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4e/Asdreni_%28portrait%29.jpg","width":395,"height":510},"pageimage":"Asdreni_(portrait).jpg"},"21886751":{"pageid":21886751,"ns":0,"title":"Grębowo","extract":"Grębowo [ɡrɛmˈbɔvɔ] (German: Grambow) is a village in the administrative district of Gmina Kamień Pomorski, within Kamień County, West Pomeranian Voivodeship, in north-western Poland. It lies approximately 6 km (4 mi) south-east of Kamień Pomorski and 62 km (39 mi) north of the regional capital Szczecin.\nFor the history of the region, see History of Pomerania."},"50441582":{"pageid":50441582,"ns":0,"title":"Betong (federal constituency)","extract":"Betong is a federal constituency in Betong Division (Betong District), Sarawak, Malaysia, that has been represented in the Dewan Rakyat since 1971.\nThe federal constituency was created in the 1968 redistribution and is mandated to return a single member to the Dewan Rakyat under the first past the post voting system.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/PRN_Sarawak_2021.svg/500px-PRN_Sarawak_2021.svg.png","width":500,"height":365},"pageimage":"PRN_Sarawak_2021.svg"},"41303818":{"pageid":41303818,"ns":0,"title":"Magyar Demokrata","extract":"Magyar Demokrata (Hungarian pronunciation: [ˈmɒɟɒr ˈdɛmokrɒtɒ], Hungarian: Hungarian Democrat) is a weekly political magazine published in Budapest, Hungary. It has been in circulation since 1997.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/70/Magyar_Demokrata_logo.png","width":350,"height":145},"pageimage":"Magyar_Demokrata_logo.png"},"55701471":{"pageid":55701471,"ns":0,"title":"Lynchburg Hosiery Mill No. 1","extract":"The Lynchburg Hosiery Mill No. 1 is a historic industrial property at 2734 Fort Avenue in Lynchburg, Virginia.  The 4-acre (1.6 ha) property includes two early 20th-century brick buildings whose construction history dates to 1900, although the oldest surviving portions now date to the 1920s.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Lynchburg_Hosiery_Mill_No._1.jpg/500px-Lynchburg_Hosiery_Mill_No._1.jpg","width":500,"height":332},"pageimage":"Lynchburg_Hosiery_Mill_No._1.jpg"}}}}
