2026-06-04 15:46:11 [http-nio-8080-exec-6] DEBUG c.d.w.s.e.WikipediaIngestionService - Wikipedia API response body: {"batchcomplete":"","continue":{"grncontinue":"0.447904882723|0.447906646395|16026345|0","continue":"grncontinue||"},"query":{"pages":{"43544539":{"pageid":43544539,"ns":0,"title":"All That I Am (novel)","extract":"All That I Am is Australian writer Anna Funder's first fictional work, published in 2011 by Penguin Books. It follows characters affected by the Nazi regime in pre-war Germany and Britain."},"66255146":{"pageid":66255146,"ns":0,"title":"1938 Birthday Honours (New Zealand)","extract":"The 1938 King's Birthday Honours in New Zealand, celebrating the official birthday of King George VI, were appointments made by the King to various orders and honours to reward and highlight good works by New Zealanders. They were announced on 9 June 1938.\nThe recipients of honours are displayed here as they were styled before their new honour."},"60885780":{"pageid":60885780,"ns":0,"title":"The Louis Bellson Explosion","extract":"The Louis Bellson Explosion is an album by drummer Louis Bellson recorded in 1975 and released by the Pablo label."},"38465372":{"pageid":38465372,"ns":0,"title":"1955 in philosophy","extract":"1955 in philosophy"},"79600991":{"pageid":79600991,"ns":0,"title":"Herbert Whittall (footballer, born 1858)","extract":"Herbert Octave Whittall (1858 – 3 February 1929) was an Anglo-Ottoman footballer and manager of Bournabat FC in the 1890s."},"62829100":{"pageid":62829100,"ns":0,"title":"Marco García (Mexican footballer)","extract":"Marco Antonio García Robledo (born 17 January 2000), also known as Enano, is a Mexican professional footballer who plays as a midfielder for Liga de Expansión MX club Atlante."},"26523296":{"pageid":26523296,"ns":0,"title":"Maremanda","extract":"Maremanda is a village in Vissannapet mandal, located in NTR district of the Indian state of Andhra Pradesh."},"79334344":{"pageid":79334344,"ns":0,"title":"1977 Labour Party leadership election (Ireland)","extract":"The 1977 Labour Party leadership election in the Republic of Ireland began following the decision of Brendan Corish not to seek re-election as leader of the Labour Party when Dáil Éireann reconvened after the 1977 general election, where Labour lost three TDs.  Corish had led the party for over fifteen years by this point and was approaching sixty, being cited as finding politics as painful and unenjoyable, which likely contributed to his decision to stand down.  His successor was elected by the members of the Labour parliamentary party on 1 July 1977.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Frank_Cluskey%2C_1981_01_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Frank_Cluskey%2C_1981_01_%28cropped%29.jpg","width":500,"height":667},"pageimage":"Frank_Cluskey,_1981_01_(cropped).jpg"},"67282757":{"pageid":67282757,"ns":0,"title":"Pericastor","extract":"In Greek mythology, Pericastor (Ancient Greek: Περικάστωρ) was the father of Androthoe who married Peristhenes and became the mother of the fisherman Dictys and Polydectes, king of Seriphos. Otherwise, nothing is known about him."},"56532889":{"pageid":56532889,"ns":0,"title":"Stizoides foxi","extract":"Stizoides foxi, or Fox's stizoide, is a species of sand wasp in the family Bembicidae.  It is found in Central America and North America."}}}}
