2026-06-04 15:47:23 [http-nio-8080-exec-8] DEBUG c.d.w.s.e.WikipediaIngestionService - Wikipedia API response body: {"batchcomplete":"","continue":{"grncontinue":"0.286953634565|0.286955009325|53471995|0","continue":"grncontinue||"},"query":{"pages":{"20516816":{"pageid":20516816,"ns":0,"title":"Albany Theatre","extract":"The Albany is a multi-purpose arts centre in Deptford, south-east London.\nFacilities include a flexible performance space holding up to 300 seated or 500 standing and a bar, two studio theatres, a performance cafe and rehearsal / meeting rooms. The Albany currently hosts a varied programme of events including music, spoken word, theatre, club nights, and children's shows.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Albany_Theatre_in_Deptford.jpg/500px-Albany_Theatre_in_Deptford.jpg","width":500,"height":667},"pageimage":"Albany_Theatre_in_Deptford.jpg"},"22846918":{"pageid":22846918,"ns":0,"title":"Eurocode: Basis of structural design","extract":"In the Eurocode series of European standards (EN) related to construction, Eurocode: Basis of structural design (informally Eurocode 0; abbreviated EN 1990 or, informally, EC 0) establishes the basis that sets out the way to use Eurocodes for structural design. Eurocode 0 establishes Principles and requirements for the safety, serviceability and durability of structures, describes the basis for their design and verification and gives guidelines for related aspects of structural reliability. Eurocode 0 is intended to be used in conjunction with EN 1991 to EN 1999 for the structural design of buildings and civil engineering works, including geotechnical aspects, structural fire design, situations involving earthquakes, execution and temporary structures.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/EN1990.svg/500px-EN1990.svg.png","width":500,"height":500},"pageimage":"EN1990.svg"},"80731616":{"pageid":80731616,"ns":0,"title":"Siqueiranthus","extract":"Siqueiranthus is a genus of bromeliads. It includes a single species, Siqueiranthus cinereus, a perennial native to Alagoas state in northeastern Brazil.\nThe species was first described as Cryptanthus cinereus by Débora Maria Cavalcanti Ferreira and Rafael Batista Louzada in 2020."},"38160874":{"pageid":38160874,"ns":0,"title":"Samantha Bowen","extract":"Samantha Bowen (born 21 March 1986) is a former British soldier and British sitting volleyball player. Bowen was discharged from the British Army in 2008 after suffering shrapnel wounds following a mortar attack during active duty in Iraq. Bowen subsequently took up the sport of sitting volleyball and represented Great Britain at the 2012 Summer Paralympics."},"47833319":{"pageid":47833319,"ns":0,"title":"Vittorio Simonelli","extract":"Vittorio Simonelli (May 1860, in Arezzo – 9 February 1929, in San Quirico d'Orcia) was an Italian geologist and paleontologist."},"79364718":{"pageid":79364718,"ns":0,"title":"2025 Conference USA women's basketball tournament","extract":"The 2025 Conference USA women's basketball tournament was the postseason women's basketball tournament that completed the 2024–25 season in the Conference USA. The tournament was held at the Von Braun Center in Huntsville, Alabama, from March 11–15, 2025. The winner, Liberty, received the conference's automatic bid to the 2025 NCAA tournament."},"37011627":{"pageid":37011627,"ns":0,"title":"Typhoon Sanba","extract":"Typhoon Sanba, known in the Philippines as Super Typhoon Karen, was the strongest tropical cyclone worldwide in 2012. The sixteenth named storm and tenth typhoon of the annual typhoon season, Sanba formed as a tropical depression east of the Philippines on September 10. The storm gradually intensified as it moved generally northward in an area favorable for tropical development.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Sanba_2012-09-14_0101Z.jpg/500px-Sanba_2012-09-14_0101Z.jpg","width":500,"height":649},"pageimage":"Sanba_2012-09-14_0101Z.jpg"},"10447970":{"pageid":10447970,"ns":0,"title":"Santa María del Campo","extract":"Santa Maria del Campo is a town and municipality in the Province of Burgos, Spain. The village is in the wine region known as Ribera del Arlanza, 22 km from Lerma.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/NuestraSe%C3%B1oraDeLaAsunci%C3%B3nDesdeElBalc%C3%B3n-rectangular.jpg/500px-NuestraSe%C3%B1oraDeLaAsunci%C3%B3nDesdeElBalc%C3%B3n-rectangular.jpg","width":500,"height":288},"pageimage":"NuestraSeñoraDeLaAsunciónDesdeElBalcón-rectangular.jpg"},"36703461":{"pageid":36703461,"ns":0,"title":"Beejan Land","extract":"Beejan Land (Persian: بیجان لاند; born 1985 in Paddington, New South Wales, Australia) is an Australian actor and producer. He graduated from National Institute of Dramatic Art and Newtown High School of the Performing Arts\nBeejan also trained at the L'École Internationale de Théâtre Jacques Lecoq. Beejan is also a graduate of ACTT's Talented Young Actors' Program, National Institute of Dramatic Art Acting and Playwrighting programs."},"42547007":{"pageid":42547007,"ns":0,"title":"MAZ-5335","extract":"MAZ-5335 is a Soviet truck, manufactured at the Minsk Automobile Plant from 1977 to 1990.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/MAZ-500_%28Belagro-2019%29_03.jpg/500px-MAZ-500_%28Belagro-2019%29_03.jpg","width":500,"height":415},"pageimage":"MAZ-500_(Belagro-2019)_03.jpg"}}}}
