2026-06-04 15:53:39 [http-nio-8080-exec-7] DEBUG c.d.w.s.e.WikipediaIngestionService - Wikipedia API response body: {"batchcomplete":"","continue":{"grncontinue":"0.578452884145|0.578454876424|28914012|0","continue":"grncontinue||"},"query":{"pages":{"24272686":{"pageid":24272686,"ns":0,"title":"Hwanggang Dam","extract":"Hwanggang Dam (Korean: 황강댐) is a hydroelectric dam on the Imjin River in Tosan County, North Korea. Located about 26 miles (42 km) north of the Korean Demilitarized Zone, the dam has an estimated capacity of 400,000,000 short tons (360,000,000 t). Construction began in 2002 and was completed in 2007.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Pongrae_Dam.png/500px-Pongrae_Dam.png","width":500,"height":415},"pageimage":"Pongrae_Dam.png"},"3178147":{"pageid":3178147,"ns":0,"title":"Colin Murphy (ice hockey)","extract":"Colin Murphy (born April 11, 1980) is a former Canadian professional ice hockey player who played in the American Hockey League and Deutsche Eishockey Liga.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Colin_Murphy.jpg/500px-Colin_Murphy.jpg","width":500,"height":584},"pageimage":"Colin_Murphy.jpg"},"69336748":{"pageid":69336748,"ns":0,"title":"Huub de Leeuw","extract":"Huub de Leeuw (15 April 1910 – 30 June 1983) was a Dutch footballer who played as a midfielder for Willem II. He made two appearances for the Netherlands national team in 1929.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Nederlands_voetbalelftal_1929.jpg/500px-Nederlands_voetbalelftal_1929.jpg","width":500,"height":313},"pageimage":"Nederlands_voetbalelftal_1929.jpg"},"82632114":{"pageid":82632114,"ns":0,"title":"Svenja Jungo","extract":"Svenja Jungo (born 12 December 2004) is a Swiss freestyle wrestler."},"16597089":{"pageid":16597089,"ns":0,"title":"Rene Gonzalez","extract":"Rene Gonzalez may refer to:\n\nRene Gonzales (born 1960), American former professional baseball infielder\nRené González (baseball) (1918–1982), Cuban baseball player\nRene Gonzalez (politician), American politician based in Portland, Oregon\nRene Gonzalez Architects, an architecture firm\nRené González (singer) (born 1964), Puerto Rican christian music singer."},"27166824":{"pageid":27166824,"ns":0,"title":"Echoes of Valor","extract":"Echoes of Valor is an American anthology of fantasy stories, edited by Karl Edward Wagner. It was first published in paperback by Tor Books in February 1987.\nThe book collects three classic fantasy novellas by Robert E. Howard, Fritz Leiber, and Henry Kuttner."},"43476549":{"pageid":43476549,"ns":0,"title":"Malao","extract":"Malao (Ancient Greek: Μαλαὼ) was an ancient port city in present-day Somaliland. The town was situated on the site of what later would become the city of Berbera. It was a key trading center involved in the Red Sea-Indian Ocean trade during Late Antiquity.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Periplous_of_the_Erythraean_Sea.svg/500px-Periplous_of_the_Erythraean_Sea.svg.png","width":500,"height":353},"pageimage":"Periplous_of_the_Erythraean_Sea.svg"},"19045168":{"pageid":19045168,"ns":0,"title":"Gina Bianchini","extract":"Gina Bianchini (born 1972) is an American entrepreneur and investor. She is the Founder & CEO of Mighty Networks.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Gina_Bianchini_headshot.png/500px-Gina_Bianchini_headshot.png","width":500,"height":513},"pageimage":"Gina_Bianchini_headshot.png"},"70909857":{"pageid":70909857,"ns":0,"title":"Tsel, Asipovichy district","extract":"Tsel (Belarusian: Цэль, romanized: Ceĺ; Russian: Цель) is a village in Asipovichy District, Mogilev Region, Belarus. It is administratively part of Pratasevichy selsoviet. It is situated on the Svislach River, roughly 20 km (12 miles) northwest of Asipovichy and 90 km (56 miles) southeast of Minsk."},"42063996":{"pageid":42063996,"ns":0,"title":"Terminology Coordination Unit of the European Parliament","extract":"The Terminology Coordination Unit (TermCoord) is a supporting unit to the translation units of the Directorate-General for Translation (DG TRAD) of the European Parliament. TermCoord was created in 2008 by Rodolfo Maslias, professor at the Universities Luxembourg and Savoie-Mont Blanc, to stimulate and coordinate the terminology work of the 24 translation units of the European Parliament in Luxembourg.\nIt provides the terminologists and translators with tools, resources, support and training to facilitate their daily translation tasks."}}}}
