2026-06-04 16:01:00 [http-nio-8080-exec-2] DEBUG c.d.w.s.e.WikipediaIngestionService - Wikipedia API response body: {"batchcomplete":"","continue":{"grncontinue":"0.250219533196|0.250220806068|60994542|0","continue":"grncontinue||"},"query":{"pages":{"46290603":{"pageid":46290603,"ns":0,"title":"2015 Poole Borough Council election","extract":"The 2015 Poole Borough Council election took place on 7 May 2015 to elect members of Poole Borough Council in England. This was on the same day as other local elections and the Parliamentary General Election.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Poole_Borough_Council_election_2015_map.svg/500px-Poole_Borough_Council_election_2015_map.svg.png","width":500,"height":503},"pageimage":"Poole_Borough_Council_election_2015_map.svg"},"1021618":{"pageid":1021618,"ns":0,"title":"Frank Lentini","extract":"Francesco \"Frank\" Lentini (18 May 1889 − 21 September 1966) was an Italian-American sideshow performer who toured with numerous circuses. Born with a conjoined twin, Lentini had three legs.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/08/Frank_Lentini_Zusatzfu%C3%9F_%28retouched%29.jpg","width":336,"height":448},"pageimage":"Frank_Lentini_Zusatzfuß_(retouched).jpg"},"40948977":{"pageid":40948977,"ns":0,"title":"Former Geological Survey of Canada Building","extract":"The Former Geological Survey of Canada Building (French: Ancien édifice de la Commission géologique du Canada) is a three-storey, stone building located at the intersection of Sussex Drive and George Street in the Byward Market area of Ottawa, Ontario, Canada.  It is named for its former occupant, the Geological Survey of Canada.  The building was designated a National Historic Site of Canada in 1955 as it is one of the oldest remaining buildings in Ottawa, and over the years it has served as home to various public and cultural institutions.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Former_Geological_Survey_of_Canada_Building.jpg/500px-Former_Geological_Survey_of_Canada_Building.jpg","width":500,"height":277},"pageimage":"Former_Geological_Survey_of_Canada_Building.jpg"},"34845458":{"pageid":34845458,"ns":0,"title":"Palatine Court of Durham Act 1889","extract":"The Palatine Court of Durham Act 1889 (52 & 53 Vict. c. 47) was an act of the Parliament of the United Kingdom.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Coat_of_arms_of_the_United_Kingdom_%281837%29.svg/500px-Coat_of_arms_of_the_United_Kingdom_%281837%29.svg.png","width":500,"height":500},"pageimage":"Coat_of_arms_of_the_United_Kingdom_(1837).svg"},"30865072":{"pageid":30865072,"ns":0,"title":"David Seisay","extract":"David Seisay (aka MC Stranger aka D-Flex) is a Swedish-American songwriter, musician and entrepreneur who became known as a rapper in Rob'n'Raz but is also known for his career as a personal trainer. He is the founder and CEO of D-Flex House of Fitness, a company that provides health and wellness services.\nHe co-wrote the song 'One Step Closer To You' for B-Boys International and performed with them at the Swedish national selection for the 2005 Eurovision Song Contest."},"41681896":{"pageid":41681896,"ns":0,"title":"Hanacpachap cussicuinin","extract":"\"Hanacpachap cussicuinin\" (modern orthography: Hanaq pachap kusikuynin) is a processional hymn to the Virgin Mary in the Quechua language of central Peru, but in a largely European sacred music style. Composed by Juan Pérez de Bocanegra between 1620 and 1631, a Franciscan priest, published in 1631 in the Viceroyalty of Peru making it the earliest work of vocal polyphony printed in the New World.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5c/Hanacpachap_cussicuinin_%281631%29.png","width":496,"height":753},"pageimage":"Hanacpachap_cussicuinin_(1631).png"},"18012908":{"pageid":18012908,"ns":0,"title":"Game System License","extract":"The Game System License is a license that allows third-party publishers to create products compatible with and using the intellectual property from the 4th edition of Dungeons & Dragons (D&D). Wizards of the Coast (WotC) released it to the public by on June 17, 2008.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2d/Dados_4_a_20_caras_trans.png","width":420,"height":420},"pageimage":"Dados_4_a_20_caras_trans.png"},"43702923":{"pageid":43702923,"ns":0,"title":"My Girl's Pussy","extract":"\"My Girl's Pussy\" (or  simply \"Pussy!\") is a 1931 jazz song recorded by the British bandleader and clarinetist Harry Roy and His Bat Club Boys.\nThe lyrics play on the two meanings of the word pussy (i.e. cat/female genitalia) in a series of double entendres.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Harry_Roy.jpg/500px-Harry_Roy.jpg","width":500,"height":971},"pageimage":"Harry_Roy.jpg"},"60630060":{"pageid":60630060,"ns":0,"title":"Su Yu-chang","extract":"Su Yu-chang (Chinese: 蘇昱彰; pinyin: Sū Yùzhāng; (1940-06-24)24 June 1940 – (2019-04-29)29 April 2019), was a Taiwanese martial artist, scholar and practitioner of traditional Chinese medicine who devoted his life to teaching kung fu, traditional Chinese philosophy and medicine all over the world.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Su_Yu-chang_signed_Bagua_Yue.jpg/500px-Su_Yu-chang_signed_Bagua_Yue.jpg","width":500,"height":489},"pageimage":"Su_Yu-chang_signed_Bagua_Yue.jpg"},"55788296":{"pageid":55788296,"ns":0,"title":"Femi Claudius Cole","extract":"Femi Claudius Cole (born 1962) is a Sierra Leonean politician. In 2016 she founded the Unity Party, making her the first Sierra Leonean woman to form a political party. In 2018, she was the first woman to run for the office of President of Sierra Leone.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d5/Femi_Claudius_Cole_2018.jpg","width":382,"height":552},"pageimage":"Femi_Claudius_Cole_2018.jpg"}}}}
